(text "SMAJ18A is a 400 W, 10/1000 us clamp, about 29.2 V. It is not load-dump protection. A load-dump pulse is a different, much larger stress, and its source impedance is unmeasured.\\nAP6320x absolute maximum is 35 V DC and 40 V for 400 ms. Recommended operating maximum is 32 V. The TVS keeps a short pulse inside that range only while the TVS itself survives.\\nEN is tied to +12V_MCU. Internal VIN UVLO is about 3.5 V rising, 440 mV hysteresis. It is not raised, because a shared windlass battery sag is unmeasured.\\nReverse battery: Q_MCU turns off. The unidirectional TVS then conducts and F_MCU is what opens. F_5V is the 2 A anti-surge fuse Murata requires on a 5 V MEJ2 input.\\nCoil branch is now sized for two Finder 40.31 coils, 42 mA each, only one at a time. F_COIL is 1 A. Q_COIL is the same DMP6023LE. SMAJ18A on this branch is the same short-pulse clamp, not load-dump protection." (at 20 100 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "2cfa6d82-9505-4cc6-95a5-d86c2b275a50"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
